CHECK mode is one of "generate", "improve".

SET write_draft = FALSE

IF mode == "generate":
    DO Read ../be-human.md once for writing; use one plain reason sentence (usually 10–20 words), no
        code walkthrough, and 1–2 Overall Reason sentences on main effort/risk (usually under 40
        words).

    DO Search affected flow once; read relevant code/coverage together. Use initialized structure,
        not template asset; no tests.

    DO Read team scoring guidance once; otherwise use nonnegative integers: 0 = no meaningful work,
        1–3 = increasing complexity.

    DO Confirm expected behavior before choosing fixes; record Boolean scope_is_ambiguous for
        scope-changing ambiguity.

    IF scope_is_ambiguous == TRUE:
        DO Clarify scope from relevant Jira comments/attachments. Request outside-sandbox execution
            on first call (Cursor required_permissions: ["all"]); stop if denied/unavailable.

    DO Assess scope/effort/material risks; further searches must affect the estimate. Record Boolean
        estimate_is_blocked and missing information.

    IF estimate_is_blocked == TRUE:
        ASK "What is the missing scope or behavior needed for this estimate?" AS clarification

        DO Apply clarification to scope; update Boolean estimate_is_blocked and retain unresolved
            assumptions.

        CHECK estimate_is_blocked == FALSE

    DO Fill in-memory draft for the requested end state, including completed work; preserve
        supported developer decisions, six rows/order/fields/Markdown. Keep fixes conditional,
        assumptions in Risk & Unknowns, reasons in-category, zeros explained, and no
        double-counting.

    CHECK draft has complete fields, no placeholders/unsupported claims, scores following team scale
        or fallback, Total Complexity Score = six-score sum, and supported numeric Final Estimate
        ending in SP; no invented score-to-SP formula.

    SET write_draft = TRUE

IF mode == "improve":
    DO Read ../be-human.md once for writing; use one plain reason sentence (usually 10–20 words), no
        code walkthrough, and 1–2 Overall Reason sentences on main effort/risk (usually under 40
        words).

    DO Refine requested parts into in-memory draft, preserving supported decisions/layout and
        wording-only scores/scope/SP. Inspect evidence only as needed; no code investigation/Jira
        retrieval for wording edits or tests. Change SP only if breakdown/evidenced conventions do
        not support it; explain why.

    CHECK Changed fields/dependent totals are complete and supported: six rows/order/fields
        preserved, nonnegative integer team scores (fallback 0 = no work, 1–3 = increasing
        complexity), zeros explained, reasons in-category, uncertainty in Risk & Unknowns, no
        double-counting, correct score sum, and numeric supported Final Estimate ending in SP
        without invented formulas. Leave unrelated fields unchanged.

    DO Retain unrelated incomplete fields for the reply.

    SET write_draft = TRUE

IF write_draft == TRUE:
    DO Recheck ticket.md's active ID as current_ticket_id.

    CHECK current_ticket_id == ticket_id

    DO Save draft only to estimate_path.

    DO Verify the saved file once against draft.

PRINT with ticket_id, SP, file/verified URL, assumptions, unrelated gaps, justified SP changes, and
    requested explanation; brief unless asked. Preserve task files on publish; inspect remote state
    before uncertain-write retries.
